":{"precision":0.0,"recall":0.0,"f1":0.0,"tp":0,"fp":5,"fn":2,"rel_precision":0.0,"rel_recall":0.0,"rel_f1":0.0,"rel_tp":0,"rel_fp":5,"rel_fn":2},"pmid":"1928887","relations":["D002216 | CID | D009270","D009270 | CID | D062787","D002216 | CID | D062787","D009270 | CID | D007022","D002216 | CID | D007022"],"text":"Naloxone reversal of hypotension due to captopril overdose. The hemodynamic effects of captopril and other angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors may be mediated by the endogenous opioid system. The opioid antagonist naloxone has been shown to block or reverse the hypotensive actions of captopril. We report a case of an intentional captopril overdose, manifested by marked hypotension, that resolved promptly with the administration of naloxone. To our knowledge, this is the first reported case of captopril-induced hypotension treated with naloxone. Our experience demonstrates a possible role of naloxone in the reversal of hypotension resulting from captopril."}